Add a real Shopify OAuth connect flow, alongside the paste-a-token path

Shopify retired creating custom apps directly in a store's admin — new
apps now go through the Partner/Dev Dashboard and a real OAuth token
exchange rather than a static token you copy off a page. Rather than
leave the existing paste-a-token flow as the only (now partly stale)
option, this adds a proper "Connect via OAuth" button that mirrors the
Meta/Google Ads/TikTok pattern:

- /api/integrations/shopify/start takes a shop domain (its consent
  dialog lives on the store's own domain, unlike the other three
  providers' single fixed authorize URL) plus the usual signed-state
  CSRF nonce.
- /api/integrations/shopify/callback verifies both our own state AND
  Shopify's own hmac signature on the callback params, exchanges the
  code for a non-expiring offline access token, then hands off to the
  EXISTING connectShopifyStore() — the same function the paste-a-token
  form already calls — so both connect paths always produce an
  identical connection and can never drift apart.
- New SHOPIFY_CLIENT_ID/SHOPIFY_CLIENT_SECRET env vars gate it; the
  paste-a-token form's copy is updated to stop pointing at the
  discontinued in-admin flow and point at the new button instead.

tsc, lint, tests (11/11), and production build all pass clean.

